// Rule: [T1219] Msarat - Browser Cdp Remote Debugging
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1219
// Classification: Production candidate
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: A process-telemetry candidate for browser mediated command and control through headless Chrome or Edge.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for browser cdp remote debugging using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: msaRAT.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// msaRAT browser-mediated C2: headless Chrome/Edge with CDP remote debugging
// Status: Production candidate - Untested implementation sketch
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceProcessEvents
// Source evidence: Cisco Talos observed msaRAT launching Chrome or Edge in
// headless mode with a remote-debugging port so the RAT could control the
// browser through Chrome DevTools Protocol.
//
// A match does not prove msaRAT. Browser automation, synthetic monitoring,
// kiosk systems, software testing and developer debugging can use both flags.
// Validate device role, parent process, browser profile and software owner.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName in~ ("chrome.exe", "msedge.exe")
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "--headless"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "--remote-debugging-port"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountName,
          FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          SHA1, ReportId

